                 PsioMan - Psion Data Manager for Windows
===========================================================================


Instalation of the packed PsioMan
---------------------------------

For installation with  the  setup  disk  see  next  section. (There  are no 
differences in the result of the installation!)

For instalation just copy  the unpacked  files in  a new empty subdirectory
or an existing directory of a previous installed version of PsioMan. To run 
this program  you will need  VBRUN300.DLL in  the windows\system  directory 
(the runtime version  of Microsoft Visual Basic 3.0).  All other files  are 
included.  You  do  not  need  to  copy  any  files  to the  windows\system 
directory.

When  updating  from a  previous verison,  please replace  ALL files in the 
directory with the newer ones.  The Update Zip file contains only the newer
files from its direct preceeding version (1.0b -> 1.0a). 

Install the  Icon in your favourite  program manager  by using the commands
'File', 'New'.

For further information see the help file (psioman.hlp) by using one of the
following commands:
 - 'Help', 'Contents'
 - 'Help', 'News'


Instalation of PsioMan with Setup
---------------------------------

If you have received an original PsioMan Setup disk start the Setup program
named setup.exe and follow the instructions on the screen. 

When you are  asked to  Register the  program with your name and the serial 
number, choose the button "Test Version" to install the test  version.  Or, 
if  you already  have the  serial number  printed  your  disk fill  out the 
registration dialog as propted on the screen.

IMPORTANT:  If you  got a  licence / invoice  form please  install the test 
version  first,  start PsioMan  and  register  in the  running  program  by 
choosing the command Licence from the Utilities menu.

Again:   It  doesn't matter  whether you  are using  the  compressed  files 
- downloaded from a BBS - to install PsioMan or the Setup Disk.  There will 
be the same files installed at the same place.


